@base = https://favorita-api.onrender.com/api

### 1. Register on production. Expect 201
# @name reg
POST {{base}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Prod Test", "username": "prod_test", "email": "prodtest@example.com", "password": "ProdTest123" }

###
@token = {{reg.response.body.$.data.token}}

### 2. Create a product. Expect 201
POST {{base}}/products
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": "Production Test Serum",
  "brand": "Test Brand",
  "category": "skincare",
  "origin": "local",
  "price": 250,
  "description": "Created on the live API to test the deployment.",
  "links": [{ "platform": "shopee", "url": "https://shopee.ph/prod-test" }]
}

### 3. It shows up publicly. Expect total 1
GET {{base}}/products

### 4. Security headers are present. Look for content-security-policy and strict-transport-security
GET {{base}}/health

### 5. CORS: an unlisted origin gets NO access-control-allow-origin header
GET {{base}}/products
Origin: https://evil.example